# Shelldock Isle: "You may play the exiled card without paying its mana cost if a library has twenty or fewer cards in it".
# Bot1's library has thirty-odd cards and Bot2's has twenty-one on turn 3 (29 cards, seven in its hand, one drawn on turn 2), so the
# condition is false when the ability resolves and the Black Lotus hidden on turn 1 stays in exile. (The neighbouring
# scenario, with Bot2's library at exactly twenty, is the positive control.)
[Bot1 Deck]
Shelldock Isle
Mox Sapphire
Island x5
Black Lotus
Island x3
Island x30

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x29

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Shelldock Isle.Play
Bot1.Arrange(Black Lotus | Island; Island; Island)
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Shelldock Isle.Activate(Ability: {U}, {T}: You may play)

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Shelldock Isle; Mox Sapphire
Exile.Count = 1
